```
Title: Potential WSL InstallLocation Registry Key Modification
Author: Liran Ravich, Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
Date: 2026-05-05
Level: medium
Description: Detects modifications to the Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL) InstallLocation registry key.
 Attackers can modify this registry key to redirect the execution flow of legitimate WSL processes (wsl.exe or bash.exe) to a malicious payload, acting as a proxy execution and defense evasion technique.
MITRE Tactic: Persistence
Tags: attack.stealth, attack.defense-impairment, attack.persistence, attack.t1112, attack.t1218
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_wsl_installlocation_registry_key_modification.yml
 False Positives:
   - Unlikely
```
TargetObject="*\\Lxss\\MSI\\InstallLocation*" NOT (Details IN ("C:\\Program Files\\WSL", "%ProgramFiles%\\WSL") OR Details IN ("*:\\Program Files\\WindowsApps\\MicrosoftCorporationII.WindowsSubsystemForLinux_*", "*\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\WindowsApps*", "*%ProgramFiles%\\WindowsApps\\MicrosoftCorporationII.WindowsSubsystemForLinux_*") OR Image IN ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\msiexec.exe", "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\msiexec.exe"))